# Outputs Section

## Purpose

Defines the Outputs section of the MAM specification. The section acts as a contract between the module and its consumers and specifies what data the module produces.

## Inputs

| Name | Type | Required | Description |
|------|------|----------|-------------|
| content | string | Yes | Full MAM module text that contains the section |
| outputs | list | No | Output definitions to validate directly |

## Outputs

| Name | Type | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| outputs | list | Extracted output definitions |
| valid | bool | Whether the section passes validation |
| errors | list | Validation errors found in the outputs |

## Capabilities

### validate

Checks table format, columns, types, and unique names.

### extract

Pulls the output definitions out of the section table.

### document

Renders the outputs into a documentation fragment.

## Rules

- Use a Markdown table format.
- Include the Name, Type, and Description columns.
- Use valid type names from the type reference.
- Give each output a unique name.
- Use snake case for output names.
- Document every output with a description.
- Document any side effects.

## Workflow

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[Content] --> B[Validate Table]
    B --> C[Extract]
    C --> D[Document]
    D --> E[Output]
```

## Python

```python
import re

VALID_TYPES = {"string", "int", "float", "bool", "dict", "list",
               "object", "any", "null", "file", "datetime", "json", "bytes"}

def validate_type(type_name: str) -> bool:
    return type_name in VALID_TYPES

def validate_name(name: str) -> bool:
    return bool(re.match(r"^[a-z][a-z0-9_]*$", name))

def extract_outputs(content: str) -> list:
    outputs = []
    in_table = False
    for line in content.split("\n"):
        if line.strip().startswith("| Name"):
            in_table = True
            continue
        if in_table and line.strip().startswith("|"):
            if "---" in line:
                continue
            parts = [p.strip() for p in line.split("|")[1:-1]]
            if len(parts) >= 3:
                outputs.append({
                    "name": parts[0],
                    "type": parts[1],
                    "description": parts[2],
                })
        elif in_table:
            in_table = False
    return outputs

def validate_outputs(outputs: list) -> list:
    errors = []
    seen = set()
    for item in outputs:
        if not validate_name(item["name"]):
            errors.append("Invalid name: " + item["name"])
        if not validate_type(item["type"]):
            errors.append("Invalid type: " + item["type"])
        if item["name"] in seen:
            errors.append("Duplicate output: " + item["name"])
        seen.add(item["name"])
    return errors

def document_outputs(outputs: list) -> str:
    docs = "## Output Values\n\n"
    for item in outputs:
        docs += "- " + item["name"] + " (" + item["type"] + "): " + item["description"] + "\n"
    return docs
```

## Tests

### Input

```yaml
content: |
  ## Outputs

  | Name | Type | Description |
  |------|------|-------------|
  | result | string | Processing result |
  | success | bool | Whether the operation succeeded |
```

### Expected

```yaml
valid: true
errors: []
```

```python
def test_outputs():
    content = ("| Name | Type | Description |\n"
               "|------|------|-------------|\n"
               "| result | string | Processing result |")
    parsed = extract_outputs(content)
    assert parsed[0]["name"] == "result"
    assert validate_type("string")
    assert validate_name("result")
    assert validate_outputs(parsed) == []
    assert "Output Values" in document_outputs(parsed)
```

## Examples

### Simple Outputs

```markdown
| Name | Type | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| result | string | Processing result |
| success | bool | Whether the operation succeeded |
```

### Error Outputs

```markdown
| Name | Type | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| success | bool | Whether the operation succeeded |
| error | string | Error message if failed |
| error_code | string | Error code if failed |
```

